{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524378-thoughts-on-blood-sigils","id":1524378,"title":"Thoughts on Blood Sigils?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-21T21:12:13-07:00","id":1524378,"title":"Thoughts on Blood Sigils?","content":"Haven't seen much discussion on Blood Sigils besides the past on the Vienna Recovery Zone. What are your reactions to the book? In my opinion there was definitely a Requiem influence in the various artifacts and mysteries. I felt a lot of space was overused on describing the redworking scene in general. I would rather have seen more discussion on the various clans and their approach to blood sorcery. The stuff on Goratrix and the Tremere just had me shaking my head in confusion. While I appreciated getting more rituals, I had hoped to see more adaptations of older paths. Wasn't thrilled with the layout as far as mixing all the rituals of the various blood sorceries. The book has some interesting stuff but overall I wish they hadn't used so much word count on various NPCs and focused on more details on the different approaches to blood sorcery and more rituals/paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T03:50:53-07:00","id":1524382,"title":"","content":"Stylistically those sections where these supplements just list categories of people and then you get very short descriptions with stat-blocks are always a dry read but I don't think you needed the huge amount of these type of write-ups in this book. More stuff that is a story-seed or more stuff about the Clans would've been more interesting, I feel like.<br /> <br /> That section of &quot;Making the Scene&quot; spends way too much space on something as simple as &quot;Put PCs, important NPCs and locations on a relationship-map&quot;. Not only is the resulting image just unhelpful in how it turns into an assault on the eyes when you try to decipher it but that section's new &quot;Heat-tracker&quot;-system is bad. So you have these &quot;Trends&quot; in the setting supposedly and they all get a five-dot (the amount can vary) &quot;Heat-tracker&quot;. Those are important things happening in the setting, PC-projects, important NPCs hanging around... stuff like that. But then this &quot;Heat-tracker&quot; is treated like a Health-tracker and you mark both superficial and aggravated damage on it which is supposed to represent the Trend &quot;cooling off&quot;. But then there are various ways for PCs to &quot;heal&quot; superficial or aggravated damage on those trackers. And what &quot;cooling off&quot; means also could be all sort of stuff. Honestly one is better off just cribbing clocks from Blades In The Dark rather than trying to wrangle this system. Just track what PCs actually are trying to do or turn something happening in the background into a countdown. Really no need to come up with all these &quot;ifs&quot; and &quot;buts&quot; about superficial and aggravated damage on that tracker.<br /> <br /> But the sections on creating your own Blood Sorcery Rites and Thin Blood Alchemy powers is a good addition. And if you want a Chronicle focused on occult stuff in your V5 game it's a good book, I think. I certainly like this one more than Second Inquisition or the Sabbat book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}